WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
When a nonprofit you fund loses another funding source, its work

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.660
can be interrupted.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:12.100
A funding pipeline helps it plan other options before that happens.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.120
Sharke supports a group of five or ten nonprofits for a

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:15.940
year.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.200
Within ten business days of the agreed start, you receive an

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.460
initial brief.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.020
It shows how much funding each nonprofit needs and what information

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.060
still needs checking.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.320
It also lists grants open now that each nonprofit could pursue,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.860
with amounts and deadlines.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.400
Each nonprofit gets a funding pipeline: a plan of grants to

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.800
pursue and funders to approach.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.660
We deliver the plan for each quarter during the month before

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.840
it starts.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.900
We keep deadlines and next steps up to date throughout the

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.840
year.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.780
Each nonprofit provides its program information and writes and submits its

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.460
own applications.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.620
The organizations and figures in this sample report are fictional.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.580
Your first progress report arrives at month three.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.920
It shows the grants and funders being pursued, deadlines, next steps,

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.680
and funding still needed.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.260
At month six, we review progress with you and the participating

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.560
nonprofits.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.860
We decide which funding gaps to focus on, which grants to

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.920
pursue next, and which funders to contact.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.600
Support continues, with progress reports at months nine and twelve.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.640
Over the year, each nonprofit learns how to work out how

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.460
large its funding pipeline needs to be to meet its funding

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.360
goal.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.800
Its team also gets practice choosing grants to pursue, planning applications,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.740
and following up with funders.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.480
The goal is to finish the year better able to manage

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.160
that work on its own.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.240
You also receive an annual report to help with budget and

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.600
strategy planning.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.800
It brings together funding patterns, local needs, and the activities nonprofits

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.560
have reported.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:51.800
I've worked as a strategy consultant for Fortune 500 and FTSE

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.340
100 companies, and as a technology executive and an investor.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.700
Across those roles, I helped businesses decide where to put their

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.920
time and money.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.200
I've also done the grant work firsthand, winning more than one

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.720
million dollars in federal funding across several awards.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.580
I founded Sharke to help nonprofits build a pipeline capable of

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.480
funding their mission.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.180
We work out how big that pipeline needs to be, find

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.880
the right funding opportunities, and support the work needed to pursue

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.420
and win them.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.520
The price for ten nonprofits is nine thousand five hundred dollars

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.960
for the year.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.520
For five nonprofits, it is five thousand and twenty-five dollars.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.500
The participating nonprofits pay nothing.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.380
Choose five or ten nonprofits you'd like us to support.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:39.680
We'll prepare a written proposal explaining their funding needs, what Sharke

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.060
will do, what the nonprofits will do, and the price for

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:43.920
the year.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.960
You have no commitment until you receive and agree to the

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.320
invoice for the twelve-month program.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.780
Visit Sharke dot A I slash foundations to request a proposal

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.900
for the nonprofits you support.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.120
We'll set out the work and annual price, helping them build

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.700
stronger funding pipelines to sustain their missions.
